Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:41:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] mediatek: an8855: disable PHY EEE as a 6.18 RFT workaround

Linux 6.18 has substantially different phylink-managed EEE handling
from the 6.6 kernel on which this AN8855 downstream driver was first
used. The AN8855 DSA driver does not yet describe managed LPI support
through the modern phylink interface.

For RFT purposes, explicitly disable EEE at the AN8855 internal PHYs.
This mirrors the conservative approach used by other switch PHY drivers
when MAC-side EEE/LPI support has not been validated.

This patch is intentionally separate from the PMCR/vendor-fix patch so
it can be A/B tested.

---
 .../mediatek/files-6.18/drivers/net/phy/air_an8855.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/target/linux/mediatek/files-6.18/drivers/net/phy/air_an8855.c b/target/linux/mediatek/files-6.18/drivers/net/phy/air_an8855.c
index cf10b7a9a89e..333333333333 100644
--- a/target/linux/mediatek/files-6.18/drivers/net/phy/air_an8855.c
+++ b/target/linux/mediatek/files-6.18/drivers/net/phy/air_an8855.c
@@ -137,6 +137,12 @@ static int an8855_config_init(struct phy_device *phydev)
 	struct device *dev = &phydev->mdio.dev;
 	int ret;
 
+	/* RFT: keep EEE out of the equation until AN8855's MAC-side LPI
+	 * behaviour has been validated with Linux 6.18 phylink.
+	 */
+	phy_disable_eee(phydev);
+	dev_info(dev, "AN8855-RFT: EEE disabled for PHY address %d\n", phydev->mdio.addr);
+
 	/* Enable HW auto downshift */
 	ret = an8855_set_downshift(phydev, DOWNSHIFT_DEV_DEFAULT_COUNT);
 	if (ret)
